since Tesla unveiled its 35 thousand  dollar car so many of our questions have  been answered it's fast it's roomy it  has a long range and it's hot but there  are still two huge questions that remain  number one can Tesla build it on time  Tesla has a long history of the latest  every time the company unveils a new car  and begins taking reservations Elon Musk  gives a projected launch day and every  single time Tesla has missed these  deadlines most recently coming in within  18 months behind schedule the second  question is even more critical for Tesla  can the model 3 be profitable Tesla has  been burning through billions of dollars  to get ready for this car and if the  model 3 can't be profitable at its 35  thousand dollar price point there are  going to be problems Tesla needs to cut  costs and for an electric car that means  reducing the price of the battery  battery prices in general have been  falling fast the Tesla still needs to  shave off another thirty percent or so  for the muddle three numbers to work out  that's why the company is building the  world's biggest battery factory the  first stage is already producing packs  ahead of schedule and when the final  stage is complete it will have the  largest footprint of any building on the  planet there are still so many things  that must go right for Tesla in the next  two years but the company's existential  questions have changed the biggest  challenge is no longer about how to  convince drivers to go electric they've  clearly already done that now it's about  how to meet the overwhelming demand for  the model 3
 

